              %p 15 Jan 2024
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Lambert"}> Neil Lambert
                \:
              %p
                %strong Non-Relativistic M2-Branes and AdS/CFT
              %p
                slides:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Lambert-NonRelM2BranesAndADSCFT.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://cdnapisec.kaltura.com/html5/html5lib/v2.73.2/mwEmbedFrame.php/p/1674401/uiconf_id/23435151/entry_id/1_mtb4zktr?wid=_1674401&iframeembed=true&playerId=kaltura_player&entry_id=1_mtb4zktr"} kt
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.14955"} arXiv:2401.14955
              %blockquote
                %p
                  We discuss a peculiar limit of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
                  that leads to a non-relativistic
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ABJM+model"} Chern-Simons-matter theory
                  with an infinite dimensional spacetime
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry+group"} symmetry group
                  and whose dynamics leads to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
                  on a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+moduli+space"} Hitchin moduli space
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} gravitational dual
                  which is described by an eleven-dimensional Membrane-Newton-Cartan theory about a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+field"} background
                  with an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi AdS
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_2
                  factor.
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#Shahbazi2024
              %p 15 Jan 2024
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Shahbazi"}> Carlos Shahbazi
                \:
              %p
                %strong The Differential Geometry and Topology of Four- Dimensional Universal Supergravity
              %p
                slides:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Shahbazi-MTheoryAndMath2024.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://cdnapisec.kaltura.com/html5/html5lib/v2.73.2/mwEmbedFrame.php/p/1674401/uiconf_id/23435151/entry_id/1_vuc7b5h2?wid=_1674401&iframeembed=true&playerId=kaltura_player&entry_id=1_vuc7b5h2"} kt
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "pre-metric+electromagnetism#LazaroiuShahbazi23"} arXiv:2101.07236
              %blockquote
                %p
                  Using the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+cohomology"} cohomology
                  of the appropriate
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+sheaf"} locally constant sheaf
                  I will explain how to implement the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac-Schwinger-Zwanziger integrality condition
                  on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+supergravity"} four-dimensional
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical
                  ungauged
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
                  and how to interpret it geometrically in order to obtain its
                  = succeed "-covariant," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} duality
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge-theoretic
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential-geometric
                  global model. Using this construction, I will prove that
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+supergravity"} four-dimensional
                  bosonic un
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauged+supergravity"} gauged
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
                  is completely determined by a choice of polarized Siegel bundle defined over the total space of a vertically
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submersion"} submersion
                  equipped with a complete
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ehresmann+connection"} Ehresmann connection
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-duality condition
                  for connections on the underlying polarized Siegel bundle. Furthermore, I will explore the continuous and arithmetic
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
                  groups of the theory, characterizing them through
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequences"} short exact sequences
                  and realizing the latter through the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
                  of the underlying Siegel bundle acting on its
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+bundle"} adjoint bundle
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
                  and justifies the miraculous existence of U-dualities by describing them as a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
                  of the appropriately defined
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li
              %p 15 Jan 2024
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mario+Garcia-Fernandez"}> Mario Garcia-Fernandez
                \:
              %p
                %strong Gauge Theory for String Algebroids
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://cdnapisec.kaltura.com/html5/html5lib/v2.73.2/mwEmbedFrame.php/p/1674401/uiconf_id/23435151/entry_id/1_0dgm9qkk?wid=_1674401&iframeembed=true&playerId=kaltura_player&entry_id=1_0dgm9qkk"} kt
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "string+algebroid#GarciaFernandezRubioTipler"} arXiv:arXiv:2004.11399
              %blockquote
                %p
                  In this talk I will explain a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moment+map"} moment map
                  construction for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+algebroids"} string algebroids
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Courant+algebroids"} Courant algebroids
                  which arise as
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+algebroids"} Atiyah algebroids
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} higher principal bundles
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
                  of solutions, and assume a technical condition which is fulfilled in examples. We prove that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
                  carries a pseudo-Kähler metric with Kähler potential given by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dilaton"} dilaton
                  functional, a topological formula for the metric, and an infinitesimal Donaldson-Uhlenbeck-Yau type theorem. Based on joint work with Rubio and Tipler in
                  %a{:href => "string+algebroid#GarciaFernandezRubioTipler"} arXiv:arXiv:2004.11399
                  (to appear in JDG) and ongoing joint work with Álvarez-Cónsul and Tellez.
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#Giotopoulos2024
              %p 15 Jan 2024
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grigorios+Giotopoulos"}> Grigorios Giotopoulos
                \:
              %p
                %strong Towards Non-Perturbative Lagrangian Field Theory via the Topos of Smooth Sets
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://cdnapisec.kaltura.com/html5/html5lib/v2.73.2/mwEmbedFrame.php/p/1674401/uiconf_id/23435151/entry_id/1_z8xmdmu5?wid=_1674401&iframeembed=true&playerId=kaltura_player&entry_id=1_z8xmdmu5"} kt
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "smooth+set#GiotopoulosSati23"} arXiv:2312.16301
              %blockquote
                %p
                  Any notion of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+field+theory"} non-pertubative
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+geometry"}> pre
                  )-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theories"} classical field theories
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theoretic
                  contexts, presupposes a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"} convenient category
                  within which non-pertubative classical field theory may be rigorously formalised. In this talk, I will describe
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
                  as a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+spaces"} generalized smooth spaces
                  = succeed "\u201D." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} manifolds
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} of sheaves
                  over the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
                  of
                  = succeed "\u201D." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"} variational algorithm
                  of (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+field"}> bosonic
                  )
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical field theory
                  and the space of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
                  naturally take place in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} infinitesimal
                  (pertubative) structure,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermionic+fields"} fermionic fields
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+symmetries"} internal symmetries
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#Alfonsi2024
              %p 15 Jan 2024
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luigi+Alfonsi"}> Luigi Alfonsi
                \:
              %p
                %strong Towards Non-Perturbative BV-Theory via Derived Geometry and the Puzzle of Quantisation
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://cdnapisec.kaltura.com/p/1674401/sp/167440100/embedIframeJs/uiconf_id/23435151/partner_id/1674401?iframeembed=true&playerId=kaltura_player&entry_id=1_jtvq9kmw"} kt
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "BV-BRST+formalism#AlfonsiYoung23"} arXiv:arXiv:2307.15106
              %blockquote
                %p
                  In this talk I will introduce and discuss a global geometric framework which allows one to encode a natural
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+field+theory"} non-perturbative
                  generalisation of classical
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-formalism"} Batalin–Vilkovisky(BV-)theory
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative
                  = succeed "." do
