          %ul
            %li#Sen2023
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                \:
              %p
                %strong D-instanton amplitudes in string theory
              %p
                slides:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Sen-MTheoryMath2023.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I9_OaFW9KHw"} YT
              %p
                cf.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.02981"} arXiv:2204.02981
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.07138"} arXiv:2207.07138
              %blockquote
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+instanton"} D-instantons
                  give
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+contribution"} non-perturbative contribution
                  to
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+amplitudes"} string amplitudes
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/world-sheet"} world-sheet
                  theory of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+strings"} closed strings
                  gives a systematic procedure for computing these amplitudes, the analysis runs into
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infrared+divergences"} infrared divergences
                  that do not have any known cure within the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/world-sheet"} world-sheet
                  formalism. We describe how
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+field+theory"} string field theory
                  cures these divergences and gives an unambiguous procedure for computing
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+instanton"} D-instanton
                  correction to
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+amplitudes"} string amplitudes
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#Lambert2023
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Lambert"}> Neil Lambert
                \:
              %p
                %strong A non-Lorentzian View of the M5-brane
              %p
                slides:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Lambert-MTheoryMath2023.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SlEYRaq2AO8"} YT
              %p
                cf.:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.06968"} arXiv:2011.06968
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.07717"} arXiv:2212.07717
              %blockquote
                %p
                  In this talk we will discuss a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path-integral"} path-integral
                  formulation of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D6+N%3D%282%2C0%29+SCFT"} (2,0) theory
                  based upon a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian
                  without
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+invariance"} invariance
                  but a novel
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(1,3)
                  spacetime symmetry. This provides a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UV+completion"} UV complete
                  five-dimensional
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} field theoretic
                  description that we will argue admits a six-dimensional Lorentz invariance at
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} strong coupling
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#Tsimpis2023
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dimitrios+Tsimpis"}> Dimitrios Tsimpis
                \:
              %p
                %strong Universal accelerating cosmologies from 10d supergravity
              %p
                slides:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Tsimpis-MTheoryMath2023.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LEiqYz-G34g"} YT
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.10813"} arXiv:2210.10813
              %blockquote
                %p
                  4d
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FRW+model"} Friedmann-Lemaître-Robertson-Walker cosmologies
                  are obtained from time-dependent
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} compactifications
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} Type IIA 10d supergravity
                  on various classes of 6d manifolds. These cosmologies are universal in that they do not depend on the detailed features of the compactification manifold, but only on the properties which are common to all the manifolds belonging to that class. Once the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
                  are rewritten as an appropriate
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamical+system"} dynamical system
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+inflation"} expansion
                  is made manifest. Some of the resulting cosmologies exhibit eternal or semi-eternal acceleration, whereas others allow for a parametric control on the number of
                  = succeed "-foldings." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{e}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Big+Bang"} Big Bang
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singularities"} singularities
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable+universe"} universe
                  is contracting in the cosmological past (
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \lt 0
                  ), expanding in the future (
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \gt 0
                  ), while in the vicinity of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T = 0
                  it becomes
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Sitter+spacetime"} de Sitter
                  in hyperbolic slicing. We also obtain several cosmologies featuring an infinite number of cycles of alternating periods of accelerated and decelerated expansions.
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#Mathai2023
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Varghese+Mathai"}> Varghese Mathai
