              %p
                %strong Graded T-duality with H-flux for 2d sigma models
              %p
                slides:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Han-MTheoryMath2023.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.03134"} arXiv:2207.03134
              %blockquote
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
                  in
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
                  can be realised as a transformation acting on the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
                  fields in the two-dimensional nonlinear
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+model"} sigma model
                  %a{:href => "topological+T-duality#BouwknegtEvslinMathai04"} Bouwknegt-Evslin-Mathai
                  established the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+T-duality"} T-duality in a background flux
                  for the first time upon compactifying spacetime in one direction to a principal circle by constructing the T-dual maps transforming the twisted cohomology of the dual spacetimes. In this talk, we will describe our recent work on how to promote the T-duality maps of Bouwknegt-Evslin-Mathai in two aspects. More precisely, we will introduce (1) graded T-duality, concerning the graded T-duality maps of all levels of twistings; (2) the 2-dimensional sigma model picture, concerning the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iterated+loop+space"} double
                  loop space of spacetimes. This represents our joint work with Mathai.
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#Saemann23
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Saemann"}> Christian Saemann
                \:
              %p
                %strong Geometric and Non-Geometric T-duality with Higher Bundles
              %p
                slides:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Saemann-MTheoryMath2023.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i4-ohJ_Z-t8"} YT
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.01783"} arXiv:2204.01783
              %blockquote
                %p
                  I will introduce the notion of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjusted+Weil+algebra"} adjusted curvatures
                  for
                  = succeed "." do
