              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.10709"} arXiv:1906.10709
              %blockquote
                %p
                  Some time ago,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D14+supersymmetry"} Bars and Sezgin proposed
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} super Yang-Mills theory
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mi s
                        %mo +
                        %mi t
                        %mo =
                        %mn 11
                        %mo +
                        %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=s+t=11+3
                  space-time dimensions, with an electric 3-brane that generalizes the 2-brane of M-theory. More recently, Rios, Chester and the speaker found an infinite family of “exceptional” super Yang-Mills theories in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo =
                          %mi s
                          %mo +
                          %mi t
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 8
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mn 3
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=s+t=(8n+3)+3
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo =
                          %mn 3
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=3
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo =
                          %mn 27
                          %mo +
                          %mn 3
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=27+3
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mn 11
                        %mo +
                        %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=11+3
                  and can reproduce super Yang-Mills theory in D=
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 11
                        %mo +
                        %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 11+3
                  \. Upon reduction to
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo =
                          %mn 26
                          %mo +
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=26+2
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 10
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 10+2
                  worldvolume signature. A single time projection gives a
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 10
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 10+1
                  worldvolume signature, and it can serve as a model for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mn 10
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=10+1
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
                  as a reduction from the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mn 26
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=26+1
                  signature of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+M-theory"} bosonic M-theory
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Horowitz"} Horowitz
                  and
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"} Susskind
                  = succeed "," do
